=begin pod

=head1 NAME

B<ZipModule> - Use this module's 'zip-module' program  to aid development of a Raku module with ChatGPT

=head1 SYNOPSIS

This module provides Raku program C<zip-module> to 
safely collect the standard data created in an
C<App::Mi6>-managed package into a C<zip> file
without inadvertently including private data
hidden in other files (such as .git).

The target user is working on a new module and is using ChatGPT (or
another AI agent) to assist. In a 
common scenario, ChatGPT will want the current state of the user's
code or the user wants to ensure ChatGPT has his or her current code.

=head1 DESCRIPTION

This module provides Raku program C<zip-module> to 
safely do that without accidentally including any git
data or private data in the process. 

Use of this module assumes the user is a developer
creating a module using the standard layout created by C<Mi6::Helper>
or C<App::Mi6> as shown here:

=head2 Files

=begin code
    Changes LICENSE META6.json dist.ini
=end code

=head2 Directories

=begin code
    lib/ bin/ docs/ sbin/ t/ xt/ .github/
=end code

=head1 Example

=item Copy a module directory

=begin code
zip-module </path/to/Some-Module>
See zipped module "./Some-Module-SAFE.zip"
=end code

Then, using the apprpiate AI agent's method, insert
the zipped safe module directory into the AI agent's data input slot.

